# Auto Skill Bootstrap (always)

## Goal
Before planning or implementation, ensure required capabilities are covered by installed project skills.

## Trigger
Run at the start of any non-trivial task, and again when new requirements/stack/domain constraints appear.

## Phases
- Exploration
- Planning/Spec
- Implementation
- Verification
- Delivery

## Engineering-first default
If task is software work (code/config/infra, API, UI, tests, CI/CD, deploy), include engineering capabilities first.

Baseline examples:
- Planning gate: `web-development` (or `frontend`/`backend`) + `architecture`, `api-design`, `security`, `performance`, `design`, `docs`
- Implementation gate: `code-quality`, `testing-unit`, `security` + stack/domain capabilities

## Gates (mandatory)
### Gate A — before plan/spec/architecture guidance
Must run bootstrap for planning capabilities and print to chat:
- `Phases:`
- `Selected capabilities:`
- `Bootstrap result summary:` from `.claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/state.json`

### Gate B — before any code/config/infra changes
Must run bootstrap for implementation capabilities and print the same 3 blocks.

## Workflow
1. Refresh local inventory:
```bash
python3 .claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/bin/update-manifest.py
```

2. Choose 3–8 capabilities (plus domain/stack caps).

3. Search candidates (no install):
```bash
python3 .claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/bin/auto-skill-bootstrap.py --no-install \
  --cap <cap1> --cap <cap2> --cap <cap3>
```

Artifacts:
- `.claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/candidates.json`
- `.claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/state.json`

4. Decision:
- allow-listed candidates → auto-install (project-local):
```bash
python3 .claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/bin/auto-skill-bootstrap.py \
  --install-allowlisted --max-per-cap 1 \
  --cap <cap1> --cap <cap2> --cap <cap3>
python3 .claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/bin/update-manifest.py
```
- non-allow-listed only → ask user first (use `AskUserQuestion`, multi-select, include `Nothing / install none`)
- if user declines capability, persist ignore:
```bash
python3 .claude/skills/auto-skill-bootstrap/bin/auto-skill-bootstrap.py --no-install \
  --cap <cap1> --ignore-cap <cap1>
```
- no candidates (`no_candidates_caps`) → report and continue without install.

## Hard rules
- Project-local installs by default (no `-g` unless user explicitly requests global).
- Never auto-install non-allow-listed skills.
- During bootstrap gate, do not proceed to main-task implementation until candidate decision is resolved.
- Re-run bootstrap when work expands into a new domain/stack.